            ],
            "text": "third loop"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " htr baby blanket is 75 x 90 cm. The hook goes into the extra loop that sits below the two normal top loops of each half treble. Both sides of the fabric look the same and the surface is flat and smooth with a subtle horizontal rib."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "DK cotton shows the flat rib most clearly. The third-loop stitch uses slightly more yarn than regular htr because the loop is a little tighter. Total yardage is around 400 g."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What you need"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "suppliesCard",
        "attrs": {
          "heading": "Materials",
          "items": [
            {
              "name": "DK cotton yarn",
              "qty": "400 g"
            },
            {
              "name": "4 mm crochet hook",
              "qty": "1"
            },
            {
              "name": "Tapestry needle",
              "qty": "1"
            },
            {
              "name": "Scissors",
              "qty": "1 pair"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Finding the third loop"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "With the right side facing and the row just completed lying flat, look at the top of each htr. You will see two front loops as normal. Tilt the work away from you slightly: the third loop is the horizontal strand running behind and below the two main loops. Insert the hook under this loop only."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Gauge"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "16 htr x 14 rows = 10 x 10 cm in DK cotton with a 4 mm hook. Third-loop htr has a slightly different tension from regular htr; check a full swatch."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Stitches used"
